The retry_after_partial opt-in is in and committed as cb93b54e, which isn't pushed yet. All four checks pass: fmt, clippy with -D warnings, build, and the full test suite. It hasn't been tried against a real Overloaded in CI yet.

Opt-in on, stdout a pipe, stub serving partial text → `overloaded_error` → `PONG`:

| | stdout | exit | requests |
|---|---|---|---|
| before | "PARTIAL_ANSWER_7Q\n" | 1 | 1 |
| after | "PARTIAL_ANSWER_7Q\n\n\nPONG\n" | 0 | 2 |

The \n\n between the partial and the answer is the separator the retry path already writes, the same bytes a terminal user sees. Since terminal behaviour was out of scope, I pinned those bytes as they are rather than changing them.

The four rows, pinned with exact assertions in `tests/print_stdout_contract.rs`:
• **Opt-in on, partial then success:** the "after" row above.
• **Opt-in off (the default):** unchanged. The existing #976 test wasn't edited and still passes.
• **Opt-in on, death before any text:** the output is exactly PONG\n.
• **Opt-in on, every attempt dies:** the run stops after 6 requests and exits non-zero. Stdout holds 6 copies of the partial, which is the worst-case price of turning this on.

What changed:
• **Config:** a new `retry_after_partial` key, off by default. `yoyo config get retry_after_partial` from the repo root prints `true (.yoyo.toml)`, and `tests/harness_logic.sh` still passes (161/0).
• **Retry rule:** the opt-in only lifts the one case #976 refuses. The doc comment states the trade: a duplicate partial on stdout instead of a lost turn.
• **Scope:** yoyo's own four retry sites use the opt-in. The retry inside the provider library (`handle_provider_retry`, #989) deliberately passes `false`, because #991 will deal with that path by preventing duplicates altogether. The comment there says so.
• **One unplanned move:** `src/prompt.rs` was already 99 lines past its allowance in the file-size check, and my edits pushed it over. Instead of raising its allowance, I moved the retry wrapper into src/prompt/retry_after_partial.rs. The file is now 3888 lines, slightly smaller than before.
• **Two checks I had to fix along the way:** `cargo fmt` wrapped the four call sites across lines, so the existing check that counts them found only one. I shortened the calls back onto one line rather than loosening that check. Clippy also rejected an unnecessary vec! in one of the new tests, which I fixed.
• Config and docs: .yoyo.toml turns the opt-in on for the evolve loop. docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md explains the default, the opt-in and its cost, and there's a short note in ARCHITECTURE.md.

Positive control: I disabled the opt-in branch and opt_in_retries_after_streamed_partial_and_succeeds failed by name. Restoring it in the same command brought it back to passing. I ran this twice, the second time after moving the wrapper, and no marker was left behind.

#997: I posted a reply with the before/after numbers, the cost and the scope decision, and left the issue open. The stub shows a mid-stream Overloaded goes through yoyo's own retry, which is the path this covers. Whether the Day-219 failure went the same way still needs a real evolve run that hits one.
